Data normalization is the process of structuring a database model by decomposing existing
structures and creating replacement references to decrease the redundancy and improve
data integrity. However, data normalization inherently applies to relational databases. In
the case of a document collection, embedded data is preferred over referential integrity. In
addition, data views that cross the boundaries of a single collection should also be
replicated on different pivots according to the design requirements.
